    {
      "id": "clm:44bdd15b6f7e7b6cc714d01dcdeb5feedeeca6fd9e8c5d1f9434d9d772c371bd",
      "text": "In the development branch, primary-driven index builds (PDIB) are resumable, including across failover (stepdown/step-up); resumability work for failover was fixed in 9.0.0-rc0. An October 2026 ticket (SERVER-136189) states that PDIB are resumable and that about 10 tests still carry stale exclusions saying they are not. This does not establish availability in any deployed release. Sources: https://jira.mongodb.org/browse/SERVER-136189 ; https://jira.mongodb.org/browse/SERVER-125827",
      "source_url": "https://jira.mongodb.org/browse/SERVER-136189",
      "also": [
        "https://example.test/withheld-reference",
        "https://jira.mongodb.org/browse/SERVER-125827"
      ],
      "validation_status": "REDACTED-PROJECTION",
      "origin_validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:07ec538bcef3cfd84504c243ce1709ab93ca7a53a25892cd63a86e992a0f6254",
        "ev:1110bd5a86fbbd7e8185565a5d5b4ab2e14155c6131de4132ff37a4e8fa16ddb"
      ],
      "remediation": {
